    "content": "# Block Ops Mission\n\n## Overview\n\nBlock Ops exists to help facilities turn regional anesthesia from a person-dependent skill set into a repeatable site-level program.\n\nThe mission is to build the system around nerve blocks: the infrastructure, workflows, roles, materials, documentation, training, and follow-through that make blocks reliable at the site level.\n\n## Working mission statement\n\n> Block Ops helps surgical facilities build repeatable, site-level regional anesthesia programs by creating the operational infrastructure around nerve blocks.\n\n## Plain-English version\n\nBlock Ops helps a facility move from \u201cwe have people who can do blocks\u201d to \u201cwe have a system that supports blocks reliably.\u201d\n\nThat system includes:\n\n- block-bay workflow\n- cart and supply structure\n- nursing roles\n- provider and staff training\n- patient education materials\n- documentation support\n- implementation bundles\n- digital references and tracking\n- ongoing program review\n\n## Why this matters\n\nA facility can have capable clinicians and still struggle to make nerve blocks reliable across the site.\n\nThe missing piece is often not one more protocol. It is the infrastructure around the work:\n\n- where blocks happen\n- who does what\n- what supplies are stocked\n- how patients are educated\n- how blocks are documented\n- how nurses are trained\n- how safety standards are reinforced\n- how the program survives turnover or inconsistency\n\nBlock Ops exists to make that structure explicit, repeatable, and easier to sustain.\n\n## What the mission does not claim\n\nThis mission does not claim guaranteed outcomes, revenue improvement, opioid reduction, faster discharge, or more cases per day.\n\nThose claims require later evidence review before they become approved Block Ops language.\n\n## Current mission test\n\nA Block Ops activity supports the mission if it makes nerve-block delivery more:\n\n- standardized\n- repeatable\n- site-adaptable\n- durable beyond any one person\n- measurable\n- easier to teach, maintain, or improve\n\n## Related Wiki pages\n\n- [[Block Ops Positioning and Core Story]]\n- [[Block Ops North Star]]\n- [[Block Ops System Architecture]]\n- [[Block Ops Wiki Classification Rules]]\n- [[Block Ops Vision]]\n- [[Pillar Model - Gold Standard Tree]]\n\n## Open questions / needs update\n\n1. Does \u201coperational infrastructure around nerve blocks\u201d feel clearer than \u201coperating system around the block program\u201d?\n2. Should the mission mention patients directly, or keep it facility/program focused?\n3. Is \u201crepeatable, site-level regional anesthesia programs\u201d strong enough as the main promise?\n4. Is this too operational, or does that fit Block Ops?\n",
    "kind": "wiki-page"
