    "content": "---\ntype: wiki-page\nstatus: current-internal-business-approved-needs-max-review\nowner: Samir\narea: digital-platform\nreviewer: Max\nsource:\n  - BlockOps/docs/PRD-dashboard-mission-control-redesign.md\n  - Block Ops Product Spec Snapshot.md\n\nupdated: 2026-07-18\n---\n# Dashboard\n\n> **Internal status \u2014 Samir business rules approved; reconciled 2026-07-18**  \n> This page is approved as the current internal Dashboard behavior. It is **not** client-facing final copy or technical implementation evidence. Max separately owns layout, data-path, and UI verification.\n\n\n## Overview\n\nDashboard is the calm internal summary home for Block Ops.\n\nIt should give Samir, Max, Adrian, and Bloq a fast read on the current milestone, what is moving, and what each person owns without feeling cluttered or spreadsheet-like.\n\nDashboard is not Mission Control. It is the summary surface that points into Mission Control when more detail is needed.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nIf the Dashboard becomes a task dump, the team loses focus. If it hides too much, the team loses awareness.\n\nThe right Dashboard should answer in seconds:\n\n- what milestone are we in?\n- how far along are we?\n- what does each person need to focus on?\n- what is blocked or locked?\n- where should I click for details?\n\n## How it works\n\n### Required top-of-page structure\n\nThe internal Dashboard should stay minimal at the top:\n\n1. **Current Milestone**\n2. **Overall Progress**\n3. **Individual Task Progress**\n\nSearch/filter controls can exist, but should not crowd the top summary.\n\n### Current Milestone card\n\nShould show:\n\n- current milestone name\n- milestone progress percentage\n- visual progress bar\n- per-person completed / total counts\n- person counts using assigned accent colors where possible\n\n### Overall Progress card\n\nShould show:\n\n- title: **Fully Operational**\n- progress percentage\n- one progress bar\n\nIt should not show detailed task counts, blocked items, or milestone breakdowns.\n\n### Individual Task Progress card\n\nShould show each person\u2019s completed / total task count without adding extra clutter.\n\nBloq appears as **Bloq (AI)** when it owns active Mission Control tasks. Its tile is internal-only and should be omitted when Bloq has no assigned active work. Bloq ownership must never appear in the client portal.\n\n## Current standard / process\n\n### Dashboard rules\n\n- Keep the Dashboard label stable.\n- Keep it visually calm and premium.\n- Use plain-English priority language.\n- Show actionable work before locked future work.\n- Do not show every task by default.\n- Use Dashboard as a shortcut into Mission Control.\n- Do not expose client-facing portal content or drafts here unless the surface is clearly internal.\n- Show **Bloq (AI)** as an internal execution owner only when it has active assigned Mission Control tasks.\n\n### Dashboard vs Mission Control\n\n| Dashboard | Mission Control |\n|---|---|\n| summary home | detailed working board |\n| scan in seconds | inspect/filter/drill down |\n| current milestone and priorities | full milestone/workflow/task graph |\n| owner focus | all tasks, locked items, dependencies |\n| calm UI | compact operational detail |\n\n## Related Mission Control workflows/tasks\n\n- M1-WIKI-07 \u2014 QA Digital Platform Wiki pages\n\n- Dashboard / Mission Control UX\n- Design Handoff to Max / Claude Design\n- Operating Rhythm\n- M1 Final System Test\n\n## Related wiki pages\n\n- [[Mission Control]]\n- [[Digital Platform Overview]]\n- [[Block Ops Operating System]]\n- [[Mission Control Rules]]\n- [[Design Handoff Process]]\n\n## Remaining technical follow-up\n\n- Confirm final card layout after Max/Claude Design returns a stable design.\n- Add screenshots once the UI stabilizes.\n\n### QA note 2026-07-08\n\nDigital Platform QA pass completed for internal Wiki buildout. This page preserves the approved boundary: Dashboard remains the internal summary surface, Mission Control remains the execution graph, the Wiki remains the governed internal reading layer, Obsidian remains the authoring/agent-mirror/continuity layer, Supabase remains canonical live state, and the client portal exposes only approved-final client-safe content. Any schema, RLS, deployment, or UI implementation claim remains Max-review-gated until verified against current source/live infrastructure.\n\n<!-- legacy-consolidation:2026-07-10-v1:start -->\n## Client-health display boundary\n\nLegacy support and churn documents describe useful signals\u2014engagement, implementation activity, unresolved support, champion continuity, access, payment, and risk\u2014but do not prove that automated scoring or alerts exist. Dashboard may summarize verified health information; [[Client Health and Retention]] owns the business process, and Max must verify any live calculation or automation.\n<!-- legacy-consolidation:2026-07-10-v1:end -->\n",
    "kind": "wiki-page"
