    "content": "# Decision Log / Historical Archive\n\n> **Internal status \u2014 M1-WIKI-09 QA pass completed 2026-07-09**  \n> Internal historical record only. Archive content is not current guidance and is **not client-facing** unless separately reviewed and approved as client-safe. Privileged legal advice, credentials, PHI, and unnecessary client/personal data must not be copied into the general archive.\n\n## Overview\n\nDecision Log / Historical Archive preserves major decisions, superseded assumptions, source evidence, and historical context without allowing stale material to become current operating truth.\n\n## Decision record standard\n\nCapture decisions that change:\n\n- product or operating direction\n- workflow, ownership, or gate rules\n- milestone definitions\n- naming or taxonomy\n- legal/compliance posture\n- client-facing visibility\n- claims and positioning\n- data/source-of-truth authority\n\nEach decision should record:\n\n- date and concise decision\n- one accountable owner\n- reason and alternatives considered\n- sensitivity/visibility classification\n- affected system, page, task, or client\n- superseded decision/source where applicable\n- follow-up and reviewer\n- links to current Wiki and Mission Control context\n\n## Archive rules\n\n- Preserve useful business history subject to approved retention, privacy/security minimization, contractual deletion duties, incident response, and legal holds.\n- Mark outdated material as archive/source only.\n- Record the superseding decision or current page.\n- Keep archive results out of client portal search, approved agents, downloads, exports, and shared links by default.\n- Mark unsupported claims **do-not-use** and exclude them from client-facing retrieval.\n- Do not summarize privileged lawyer advice in the general log; record only the approved operational decision and a controlled restricted reference.\n- Do not keep credentials, PHI, or unnecessary personal/client data in archive notes.\n\n## Current truth versus historical context\n\n- Supabase is canonical for verified live app, Wiki, Mission Control, permission, and client-portal state.\n- Obsidian may hold internal draft/context and archive narratives but must not overwrite newer verified live state.\n- Current reviewed Wiki pages explain the active standard.\n- Archive pages explain what changed and why.\n- Repository seeds describe baseline definitions and do not automatically supersede expanded live data.\n\nExamples:\n\n- old pillar/product taxonomies \u2014 archive unless explicitly restored\n- old milestone ladders \u2014 archive; current definitions include M3 external validation, M4 foundational-client completion, and M5 paid-client onboarding\n- unsupported ROI/reimbursement/outcome claims \u2014 do-not-use until evidence and required reviews approve exact wording\n- nonfinal clinical materials \u2014 internal draft until qualified clinical fact review\n- legal documents \u2014 final only after qualified-lawyer finalization for the relevant scope\n- implementation claims \u2014 current only after technical/live verification\n- client exposure \u2014 permitted only after explicit approved-final client-safe release\n\n## Final-state rule\n\nA \u201cfinal\u201d label is valid only after all required domain reviews are recorded:\n\n- qualified-lawyer finalization for legal documents and legal posture\n- qualified clinical fact review for clinical content\n- technical verification for implementation and live-system claims\n- evidence/claim review for outcome, ROI, reimbursement, and value language\n- explicit client-safe release approval before portal exposure\n\nSamir\u2019s review establishes business/operating approval where assigned; it does not replace qualified domain review.\n\n## Visibility and access\n\nArchive material defaults to internal restricted visibility. If surfaced in the internal Dashboard/Wiki, it must be clearly labeled, role-gated where needed, separated from current guidance, and excluded from client-facing routes and agents.\n\n## Related Mission Control workflows/tasks\n\n- M1-WIKI-09 \u2014 QA Legal Risk Archive and Growth Wiki pages\n- Operating Model\n- Weekly Ops Review\n- Decision Capture\n- Status Rules\n- Wiki / Compendium Migration\n- Legal and Compliance Gates\n\n## Related wiki pages\n\n- [[Decision Capture]]\n- [[Weekly Ops Review]]\n- [[Status Rules]]\n- [[Block Ops Wiki Classification Rules]]\n- [[Backup and Continuity]]\n- [[Archive Maintenance SOP]]\n\n## Open questions / needs update\n\n- Samir owns deciding which archive metadata belongs in live Supabase versus Obsidian narrative context.\n- Samir owns assigning the periodic archive-review cadence and reviewer.\n- Max should verify role-based archive visibility if archive metadata is surfaced in the internal Dashboard.\n\n### QA note 2026-07-09\n\nThis pass removes the unsafe rule that Samir review alone makes every artifact final, adds domain-specific finalization, aligns live/source authority, and strengthens retention, privilege, do-not-use, and client-leak safeguards. The page remains internal and review-gated.\n",
